\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Request flow. The agent sends a question (1); the planner turns it into a QuerySpec without seeing any data (2); the gate checks the QuerySpec against the user's grant and picks the coarsest release level (3, step 7 in the gate box is the daily release limit, ``daily budget'' in the figure); only the per-user vault reads health data, computes the answer and builds the packet (4); the packet and a receipt identifier return to the agent (5). Seven Cloudflare Workers form four trust zones: public (site, console), identity (auth), request path (edge, planner) and protected (gate, vault). The planner and the edge hold no binding to data or policy, and a test checks the bindings between Workers.}}{6}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{6}{Request flow. The agent sends a question (1); the planner turns it into a QuerySpec without seeing any data (2); the gate checks the QuerySpec against the user's grant and picks the coarsest release level (3, step 7 in the gate box is the daily release limit, ``daily budget'' in the figure); only the per-user vault reads health data, computes the answer and builds the packet (4); the packet and a receipt identifier return to the agent (5). Seven Cloudflare Workers form four trust zones: public (site, console), identity (auth), request path (edge, planner) and protected (gate, vault). The planner and the edge hold no binding to data or policy, and a test checks the bindings between Workers}{figure.caption.7}{}}
\newlabel{fig:arch@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][5][]6}{}{}{}}
